= $\$int_{0}^{1}  $\frac{dx}{(1+$x^2$)(1+$3x^2$)} = \frac{1}{2} \$int_{0}^{1}  $\frac{3(1+$x^2$)-(1+$3x^2$)}${(1+$x^2$)(1+$3x^2$)$}dx
= \frac{1}{2} \left[ \int_{0}^{1} \frac{3dx}{1+3x^2} - \int_{0}^{1} \frac{dx}{1+x^2} \right] =  \frac{1}{2} \left[ 3 \frac{\tan^{-1}(\sqrt{3}x)}{\sqrt{3}} \Big|_{0}^{1} - \tan^{-1}(x) \Big|_{0}^{1} \right] =  \frac{1}{2} \left[ \sqrt{3} \tan^{-1}(\sqrt{3}) - \tan^{-1}(1) \right] =  \frac{1}{2} \left[ \sqrt{3} \frac{\pi}{3} - \frac{\pi}{4} \right] =  \frac{1}{2} \left[ \frac{4\sqrt{3}\pi - 3\pi}{12} \right] = \frac${(4$\sqrt{3}$-3)$\pi$}{24}
